//? Title: Recursive descent: actual grammar calls, evaluated nodes and source spans
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Arithmetic text must be grouped by precedence before its operators can be
evaluated correctly. Recursive descent encodes that grouping directly in expr,
term and factor functions. The native producer now records its actual completed
syntax nodes and byte spans, replacing a hand-drawn tree unrelated to parser
state. The original six expressions remain, together with complete-token,
malformed-input and finite-arithmetic controls.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

The grammar separates additive and multiplicative precedence:
$$ E\to T((+\mid-)T)^*,\quad T\to F((*\mid/)F)^*,\quad F\to\mathrm{number}\mid(+\mid-)F\mid(E). $$
\alttext(Expression folds additive terms, term folds multiplicative factors, and factor handles signs, groups and decimal numbers.)
Each nonterminal consumes exactly its grammatical prefix and returns its
evaluated value. Binary loops fold left, so10-2-3 means(10-2)-3 and 8/4/2
means(8/4)/2. Prefix recursion binds signs at factor level; parentheses
recursively invoke the full expression rule. Induction over the produced syntax
tree proves that every stored node value matches its child operation.

Actual nodes append in completion postorder, with real child ids and original
source byte spans. Complete-input checking rejects a second decimal point or
trailing token rather than silently accepting a numeric prefix. The grammar
excludes exponents and power syntax. Runtime is linear in bytes plus actual
grammar entries, with bounded recursion and optional linear retained tree
storage. This parser is an evaluator for this explicit grammar, not a general
left-recursive grammar parser.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/recursive_descent_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/prufer.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/flow_diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/hull_algorithms.hpp>
#include <datamunge/random/sampling_analysis.hpp>
#include <iomanip>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/qr_algorithm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/lm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/arithmetic_coding.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/rbf.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/model_plot.hpp>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/recursive_descent_parser.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = a::recursive_descent_trace("1+2*3");
    const auto &root = t.nodes[t.root];
    std::print("\n| actual postorder id | source bytes | actual operator code | actual left child | actual " "right child | actual value |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.nodes.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &n = t.nodes[i];
        std::print("| {} | [{},{}) | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, n.begin, n.end,
                   int(n.operation), n.left, n.right, n.value);
    }

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual multiplication child value\n{}",
                       t.nodes[root.right].value));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual completed root operator\n{}", root.operation));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual root value / node count\n{} / {}", t.value,
                       t.nodes.size()));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/recursive_descent_tiny.svg");
}
```
